ve protein has an opportunity to diffuse away from the receptor and deliver its message for a prolonged period to its downstream target. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9BZE4","text":"Involved in the biogenesis of the 60S ribosomal subunit (PubMed:32669547). Acts as a TP53 repressor, preventing TP53 stabilization and cell cycle arrest (PubMed:20308539)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}